   - 'sk_live_CSPPROBE_MUST_NOT_APPEAR' is the csp-probe's own canary (scripts/csp-probe.mjs:175):
     a fake secret planted in a query string whose whole job is to be absent from every
     violation report. Finding it in the probe and its logs is the check working.
   - 'sk_live_51AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOp' / 'whsec_AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrSt' are fixtures in
     stripeProbeSecretHygiene.test.ts — a test whose subject is exactly this.
   - 'whsec_leakme', 'sk_live_leak', 'whsec_attacker', 'whsec_x', 'sk_live_abcdef' are
     synthetic values in billing/CSP tests.
   - The bare 'sk_live_' (16) and 'whsec_' (9) are prose naming the prefix FORMAT in
     .env.example, SERVER_SETUP.md and the audit docs.
   No value in any tracked file is credential-shaped for real: a live Stripe key is
   sk_live_ + 24+ chars of base62 and a webhook secret whsec_ + 32+.
